Patch summary:
The guest's Vulkan driver now sends an image's list of view formats
(VkImageFormatListCreateInfo; lineageos
external-mesa3d-gfxstream-image-format-list.patch), with which the host
driver can keep a mutable-format image compressed, as ANGLE's 8-bit RGBA
images are. Two kinds of image must not get the guest's list. An emulated
compressed image is created in another format, of which the listed formats
are no views. An image the guest binds to a ColorBuffer's memory must be laid
out as the ColorBuffer's own image, which has no list: with one, Honeykrisp
compresses the image and the two would read the memory differently.
diff --git a/host/vulkan/cereal/common/vk_struct_id.h b/host/vulkan/cereal/common/vk_struct_id.h
index 6c05fbc..8565360 100644
--- a/host/vulkan/cereal/common/vk_struct_id.h
+++ b/host/vulkan/cereal/common/vk_struct_id.h
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@ REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkDebugUtilsMessengerCreateInfoEXT,
                       VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_DEBUG_UTILS_MESSENGER_CREATE_INFO_EXT);
 REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkBufferCreateInfo, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_BUFFER_CREATE_INFO);
 REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkImageCreateInfo, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_CREATE_INFO);
+REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkImageFormatListCreateInfo,
+                      VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_FORMAT_LIST_CREATE_INFO);
 REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkImageFormatProperties2, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_FORMAT_PROPERTIES_2);
 REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkNativeBufferANDROID, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_NATIVE_BUFFER_ANDROID);
 REGISTER_VK_STRUCT_ID(VkExternalMemoryBufferCreateInfo,
diff --git a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp
index 5db692f..a591e31 100644
--- a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp
